<title>SWITZERLAND: Memphis top world cargo airport in August - ACI.</title>
<headline>Memphis top world cargo airport in August - ACI.</headline>
<dateline>GENEVA 1996-12-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Memphis, base of U.S. express freight carrier, Federal Express, was the world's busiest cargo airport in August 1996, said Geneva-based Airports Council International (ACI).</p>
<p>The world's 20 busiest cargo airports in August 1996, with the volume they handled, the percentage change over August 1995 and their August 1995 ranking, were as follows:</p>
<p> 1 (1)  Memphis	     164,204 tonnes  up    6.2pct</p>
<p> 2 (5)  Miami		 151,223 tonnes  up   18.0</p>
<p> 3 (2)  Los Angeles	 144,269 tonnes  up    4.4</p>
<p> 4 (3)  New York	    138,393 tonnes  up    2.5</p>
<p> 5 (6)  Hong Kong	   133,868 tonnes  up    6.7</p>
<p> 6 (4)  Tokyo-Narita	128,796 tonnes  down  3.2</p>
<p> 7 (7)  Louisville	  121,684 tonnes  down  0.8</p>
<p> 8 (8)  Frankfurt	   120,589 tonnes  up    3.5</p>
<p> 9 (10) Seoul		 109,166 tonnes  up    9.5</p>
<p> 10 (9) Chicago	     105,373 tonnes  down  0.8</p>
<p> 11(11) Singapore	   101,824 tonnes  up    9.5</p>
<p> 12(12) Anchorage	   101,528 tonnes  up   10.5</p>
<p> 13(13) London Heathrow    91,465 tonnes  up    1.2</p>
<p> 14(15) Amsterdam	    86,725 tonnes  up   15.5</p>
<p> 15(14) New York Newark    79,651 tonnes  down  2.9</p>
<p> 16(16) Paris-CDG	    76,378 tonnes  up    5.3</p>
<p> 17(20) Taipei		 68,589 tonnes  up   12.7</p>
<p> 18(-)  Dayton		 68,051 tonnes  up   24.1</p>
<p> 19(17) Dallas F/W	   67,172 tonnes  up    1.1</p>
<p> 20(19) Atlanta		66,310 tonnes  up    6.8</p>
<p>- Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax+44 171 542 5017</p>
